Now you can confidently say:  JDBC connection pool is exhausted.

But pool exhaustion is a symptom.
We still need to answer:
WHY are all 100 connections occupied?
Possible Causes:

Case A → Long-running SQL
Case B → Database is slow
Case C → Connection leak
Case D → Application traffic spike
Case E → Deadlock / transaction waiting
Case F → External service call while holding DB connection
Case G → Pool incorrectly sized

Case A — Long-running SQL
Suppose DBA gives us some queries are in long running/.
And many application threads are waiting for JDBC connections.

